<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fourth Crusade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1204">1204</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusades">Crusades</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fourth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a> was a Western expedition that, instead of reaching the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-land">Holy Land</a>, sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 1204. The crusaders established a Latin Empire, and although the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> recovered the city in 1261, the Byzantine Empire never regained its former strength.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade.jpg" alt="Fourth Crusade" width="320" height="199" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Loyset Liédet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ConquestOfConstantinopleByTheCrusadersIn1204.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The grant gradually handed much of Constantinople's maritime commerce to Venetian merchants and created the dependency that later helped make the <b>Fourth Crusade</b>'s diversion to Constantinople attractive to the Venetians.</blockquote><a href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Count Philip of Alsace died at the siege of Acre in 1191 during the Third Crusade, and Baldwin IX was a leader of the <b>Fourth Crusade</b>, which took Constantinople in 1204.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-flanders">County of Flanders · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>His son Baldwin VI, also count of Flanders as Baldwin IX, was a leader of the <b>Fourth Crusade</b>, which took Constantinople in 1204; he was elected Latin emperor but was captured by the Bulgarians at the Battle of Adrianople in 1205 and died in captivity.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-hainaut">County of Hainaut · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In April 1204, a few days before the army of the <b>Fourth Crusade</b> captured Constantinople, they seized Trebizond on the south-eastern coast of the Black Sea with troops supplied by Georgia.</blockquote><a href="/empire/empire-of-trebizond">Empire of Trebizond · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The decline of the Dnieper trade route as Byzantium weakened, especially after the <b>Fourth Crusade</b> took Constantinople in 1204, further reduced the city's wealth.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus' · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The Principality of Achaea was born of the <b>Fourth Crusade</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-achaea">Principality of Achaea · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
